 "ownerDecisions": [
  "Q-HE2S-1 = (a) (2026-10-13, owner via the lane monitor, verbatim): a harness-onion meta packet publishes the compiled seccomp programs as data files; its layer recompiles them with the pinned v3 compiler and checks them against the published digests; R10 vendors EFFECT_GATE's two files byte-identically, gate.py pins their sha256, and the seal embeds them.",
  "Q-HE2S-2 = (a), all 14 (2026-10-13, owner via the lane monitor, verbatim): a new small primary-lane meta packet publishes all 7 roles × 2 architectures plus edge registry record v2. It ALSO carries EDGE-2 (the R12 conformance-labs → harness-engineering edge record that rides the next registry-touching packet, owner A13) and W03-PLAN-AMEND-1 (the obligation-register amendment, owner Q-HE2B-2). HE-002S merges after it."
 ],
 "notes": [
  "v1's 17 artefacts are carried unchanged, statuses included: HE-002's 13 contract files were REGISTERED_BEFORE_USE when v1 was published, and HE-002 has since merged in R10, so the consumer holds them now.",
  "A program row with providerCommit null is published by its providerPacket (this packet); its commit is that packet's merge commit.",
  "The programs are data (the v3 contract's compiled filters), not implementation source, so the boundary rule holds."
 ]
}
